    {
      "id": 23,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "How to read this case",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 72,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 5
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**Choose the Registry target:** port 8080 is the regular service; port 8082 is the temporary parallelism experiment. Registry panels follow that one target. RabbitMQ and Compliance are shared, so their totals may also include other Registry instances.\n\n**Acceptance and completion differ.** A 202 is queued work; a 201 confirms a new user + outbox commit; a 200 is an idempotent replay. Process counters reset on restart. Database counts are the authoritative ledger. No-event series can be absent, and histogram p95 has gaps without observations.\n\nScrapes and refresh are every 5s; shorter peaks can be missed. Rates use 30s windows and latency/recovery charts use 1m windows. Committed Kafka consumer-group lag and CDC connector health are not collected here; live-consumer position is not a substitute for committed backlog."
      }
    }
